# Dependencies and build output
node_modules/
dist/
*.tgz

# Cloned repos used as scan targets — not ours to commit.
# Leading slash matters: an unanchored "fixtures/" would also ignore
# tests/fixtures/, which we very much do want tracked.
/fixtures/

# Scan history written into fixtures by the test suite
**/.what-it-does/

# Generated reports. demo/ is the hosted sample — regenerate with `npm run demo`
# rather than committing 1.6MB of generated HTML into the source history.
demo/
what-it-does-report.html
eriksen-report.html
report-*.html

# OS / editor noise
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# Internal working documents. They stay on disk and out of the repository:
# strategy, budget, revenue targets, the launch drafts and the design
# rationale are for the operator, not for a stranger reading the source.
DECISIONS.md
DESIGN.md
METRICS.md
LAUNCH.md
PROJECT-ERIKSEN.md

# Local editor/agent config. Points at a sibling checkout that does not exist
# in this repository, so it is confusing to anyone but the author.
.claude/
